+## Explicit Background Admission
+
+A host can also route an explicitly designated background worker to a separate
+admission URL while keeping the same model configuration. This is different from
+choosing a smaller or cheaper model. Use the existing `LLM.base_url` interface;
+no SDK provider or agent-loop change is required.
+
+The [background admission example](https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/tree/main/examples/01_standalone_sdk/60_background_admission)
+loads a working SDK LLM profile and SDK message list. It selects `/v1` for normal
+work or `/background/v1` for background work, changes the gateway credential and
+disables automatic retries. Model, output/context limits, sampling and
+`litellm_extra_body` remain in the caller's profile. The SDK's normal parameter
+conversion and capability checks still apply.
+
+```bash
+uv run python examples/01_standalone_sdk/60_background_admission/main.py llm.json messages.json
+uv run python examples/01_standalone_sdk/60_background_admission/main.py llm.json messages.json --background
+```
+
+Start the gateway separately. [Adaptive Inference v0.2.0](https://github.com/midhatn/adaptive-inference/releases/tag/v0.2.0)
+provides these routes for an existing OpenAI-compatible model server. The example's
+README includes setup, credential handling, message format and timeout guidance.
+The host selects the class; prompt text is not used to infer priority. Pass the
+returned `LLM` to an existing `Agent` when using its normal tool workflow.
+
+This optional gateway admits one active request at a time, which can reduce native
+batching concurrency. Only pending requests can be reordered or canceled before
+dispatch. An active response is drained even if its client disconnects; an ambiguous
+upstream timeout blocks further dispatch pending operator reconciliation. It does
+not provide immediate GPU-resource release or native preemption. The example uses
+Chat Completions and does not expose Responses or model-management APIs.
+
+The SDK HTTP fixture tests verify route selection and retained generation fields;
+they do not establish model quality, native scheduling performance or a speedup.
+
